  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The magnitude of <math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mtext>&#x0394;</mtext>   <mtext>0</mtext>  </msub>  </mrow></math> varies from stronger to weaker ligand. According to spectrochemical series, <math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mtext>F</mtext>   <mo>&#x2212;</mo>  </msup>  </mrow></math>is a weaker ligand while <math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>NH</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msub>  </mrow></math>is a stronger ligand. Stronger ligand gives a larger value of <math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mtext>&#x0394;</mtext>   <mtext>0</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>.</mtext></mrow></math><br>Hence, among the given complexes <math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mrow>    <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\">     <mrow>      <msub>       <mrow>        <mtext>CoF</mtext></mrow>       <mtext>6</mtext>      </msub>      </mrow>    </mfenced></mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>3</mtext><mo>&#x2212;</mo></mrow>  </msup>  </mrow></math> is expected to have lowest value of <math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mtext>&#x0394;</mtext>   <mtext>0</mtext>  </msub>  </mrow></math> value.",
